    "proximate_text": "neither the on-shift crew nor the leadership supporting them recognized, understood or addressed the risk prior to throttling the Auxiliary Condenser outlet valves in the closed direction. The potential risk to generation never entered the thinking of anyone involved in the task. Adjusting the CWP cooling flow was considered a routine task covered by procedure. Crew inexperience and the negative potential of that inexperience was not adequately considered or addressed.",
